{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/444571-speculation-mortal-splat","id":444571,"title":"Speculation: Mortal Splat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-16T11:15:31-07:00","id":444571,"title":"Speculation: Mortal Splat","content":"So the outline talks about people who have had &quot;brushes&quot; I'm assuming with the fey, and would be abductee's. <br /> <br /> So why do you think the mortal splat will be? Fae Touched? Cambions? Enchanted Mortals? Something else?<br /> <br /> Will they be more like Wolfblooded 2.0 or Ghouls 2.0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T08:43:10-07:00","id":445993,"title":"","content":"As someone who knows precious little about specifics in the rest of nWoD (aside a bit of Mage, relatively recently), what are Wolfblooded and Ghouls like? I know they're sort of the &quot;in-betweeners&quot; for Werewolves and Vampires, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> To facilitate discussion, here's the relevant bit from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">the 2e Outline</a>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2e C:tL Outline</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appendix One: Babes in the Woods \u2013 Mortal Splat<br /> 10k, Danielle.<br /> Mortal splat section. There\u2019s been a lot of discussion here. But, essentially this is \u201cpotential targets\u201d. It\u2019s those who have had a brush, who are likely to become abductees. People who, if they play into a story the right way, can be kinda awesome and beyond the normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, shots in the dark...<br /> <br /> I get a sense of someone who's had a &quot;close encounter&quot; with something of the Wyrd. From that last bit, it's possible they stepped briefly into a role that resonated with a relevant story (or picked up the capacity for such). Certainly not enough for a Kith, but possibly enough to leave a mark, granting them some suitable blessing (and/or blight) relevant to it. The danger being that such people are more likely to stand out to the Gentry. Someone who's already somewhat resonant with the Wyrd and who has the makings of a personal mythology is just more liable to catch their eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T09:28:11-07:00","id":446045,"title":"","content":"What would you call these beings and what powers might they have Gaius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:23:31-07:00","id":446126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/444571-speculation-mortal-splat?p=445993#post445993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who knows precious little about specifics in the rest of nWoD (aside a bit of Mage, relatively recently), what are Wolfblooded and Ghouls like? I know they're sort of the &quot;in-betweeners&quot; for Werewolves and Vampires, but that's about it.<br /> <br /> To facilitate discussion, here's the relevant bit from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/385867-changeling-the-lost-second-edition-outline\">the 2e Outline</a>:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, shots in the dark...<br /> <br /> I get a sense of someone who's had a &quot;close encounter&quot; with something of the Wyrd. From that last bit, it's possible they stepped briefly into a role that resonated with a relevant story (or picked up the capacity for such). Certainly not enough for a Kith, but possibly enough to leave a mark, granting them some suitable blessing (and/or blight) relevant to it. The danger being that such people are more likely to stand out to the Gentry. Someone who's already somewhat resonant with the Wyrd and who has the makings of a personal mythology is just more liable to catch their eyes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given the survivor metaphor, these would be the metaphorical people-at-risk the changelings quietly protect from their old abusers...and help the changelings remain tied to their new lives in turn, the support network.<br /> <br /> I like it.<br /> <br /> I would call these something to do with Thresholds, maybe Walkers on it. They're right at the border between human and changeling, they've seen the path to the fae world and now that they've seen it, the Gentry want to force them down it. Maybe they have access to Oaths, though not pure Pledges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T10:36:33-07:00","id":446143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/444571-speculation-mortal-splat?p=445993#post445993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who knows precious little about specifics in the rest of nWoD (aside a bit of Mage, relatively recently), what are Wolfblooded and Ghouls like? I know they're sort of the &amp;quot;in-betweeners&amp;quot; for Werewolves and Vampires, but that's about it.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> As someone was came into the WoD through Changeling, I can sympathize. Basically,<br /> <br /> \u2022Ghouls are created by Vampires through feeding them the Kindred's &quot;fuel&quot;, Vitae. They're immortal and unaging so long as they regularly receive their &quot;fix&quot; on s monthly basis( and immediately make the difference if they miss the mark) and can learn and use Vampiric Disciplines just like their masters. But that last word is key. Due to the addictive and mind-altering nature of drink straight Vitae(as opposed to drinking normal blood and then &quot;metabolizing&quot; it as Vampires do) means that the vast majority are trapped in unequal relationships based on abuse, with even the nicest ones predicated on the fact that one is the &quot;junkie&quot; and the other is the &quot;dealer&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u2022While I don't have Werewolf 2e yet, I think what I have on Wolfblooded is good. Wolfblooded are people who the Werewolves's heritage manifests strongly in(though they are not guaranteed to Change). They do not learn the Uratha's Gifts, but rather manifest Tells(not sure how many they can possess), powers that reflect their bloodline and come with a benefit and drawback(that is, one might give you Werewolf healing but also the silver vulnerability, another might allow you to turn into a wolf but forces you to do so under the Full Moon, etc.). Unlike Ghouls, they apparently explicitly retain these powers even if they gain a non-Werewolf template. <br /> <br /> Hope that helped!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}